# media-backup: give optical drives that report no serial a unique one.
#
# udisks2 builds its drive object path from vendor, model and serial, taking
# the serial from ID_SERIAL_SHORT and falling back to ID_SERIAL. Drives that
# report no serial to udev get ID_SERIAL set to their model string, so two
# identical drives produce the same object path and udisks2 merges them into
# ONE drive object.
#
# The consequence is not cosmetic. Drive.MediaAvailable then describes
# whichever drive udisks2 probed last, so drives.py reports has_media=False
# for a drive holding a disc. This machine has two PIONEER BDR-212D units:
#
#     sr2 -> /org/freedesktop/UDisks2/drives/PIONEER_BD_RW___BDR_212D_PIONEER_BD_RW_BDR_212D
#     sr4 -> /org/freedesktop/UDisks2/drives/PIONEER_BD_RW___BDR_212D_PIONEER_BD_RW_BDR_212D
#
# ID_PATH is the discriminator: it is derived from the PCI address and ATA
# port, so it is stable across reboots and distinct per physical socket.
# Verified stable across a reboot on 2026-09-07.
#
# BOTH properties must be set, because udisks2 uses them for different jobs:
#
#   ID_SERIAL_SHORT  becomes Drive.Serial, which NAMES the drive object.
#   ID_SERIAL        is the VPD used to decide WHICH block devices belong to
#                    the same drive object.
#
# Setting only ID_SERIAL_SHORT renames the shared object without splitting it,
# which measurably does not fix the bug -- both drives then share the renamed
# object. Verified on this machine 2026-09-07.
#
# This only fires when ID_SERIAL_SHORT is absent, so drives that do report a
# real serial (sr0, sr3 here) are left exactly as they are. The
# /dev/disk/by-id symlinks do not move: 60-persistent-storage.rules has
# already evaluated SYMLINK+= from the original ID_SERIAL by the time this
# rule runs at 98.
#
# Install:
#   sudo cp 98-media-backup-optical-serial.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#   sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=block --sysname-match='sr[0-9]*'

SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="sr[0-9]*", ENV{ID_SERIAL_SHORT}=="", ENV{ID_PATH}=="?*", \
    ENV{ID_SERIAL_SHORT}="$env{ID_PATH}", ENV{ID_SERIAL}="$env{ID_MODEL}_$env{ID_PATH}"
